2. Meso‑Scale Mathematics (Mechanobiology Module)

2.1 Stress Tensor Formulation

[ \sigma_{ij} = \frac{\partial P_{ij}}{\partial x_j} ]

Where (P_{ij}) is the first Piola–Kirchhoff stress tensor.

2.2 Strain Tensor

[ \epsilon_{ij} = \frac{1}{2}\left(\partial_i u_j + \partial_j u_i\right) ]

2.3 Constitutive Model (Linear Elasticity)

[ \sigma_{ij} = \lambda \epsilon_{kk}\delta_{ij} + 2\mu \epsilon_{ij} ]

Where (\lambda) and (\mu) are Lamé parameters.

2.4 Finite Element Formulation

Weak form:

[ \int_\Omega \sigma_{ij} \partial_j w_i , d\Omega = \int_\Omega f_i w_i , d\Omega ]

Mesh resolution:

[ \Delta x_{\text{meso}} \sim 10^{-6} - 10^{-4} \text{ m} ]

2.5 Intercellular Potential

[ V_{\text{local}} = V_{\text{intercell}} - \sigma_{ij} ]

Where:

[ V_{\text{intercell}} = k(d - d_0)^2 ]

3. Micro‑Scale Mathematics (Molecular Dynamics Module)

3.1 Lennard‑Jones Potential

[ V_{LJ}(r) = 4\epsilon\left[\left(\frac{\sigma}{r}\right)^{12} - \left(\frac{\sigma}{r}\right)^6\right] ]

Force:

[ F_{LJ}(r) = -\frac{dV_{LJ}}{dr} ]

3.2 Electrostatic Potential

[ V_{\text{elec}} = \frac{1}{4\pi\epsilon_0}\sum_{i,j} \frac{q_i q_j}{r_{ij}} ]

Force:

[ F_{\text{elec}} = -\nabla V_{\text{elec}} ]

3.3 Velocity Verlet Integrator

[ \mathbf{r}(t+\Delta t) = \mathbf{r}(t) + \mathbf{v}(t)\Delta t + \frac{1}{2}\mathbf{a}(t)\Delta t^2 ]

[ \mathbf{v}(t+\Delta t) = \mathbf{v}(t) + \frac{1}{2}[\mathbf{a}(t) + \mathbf{a}(t+\Delta t)]\Delta t ]

